// expect: 134 trap: a precondition failed at lists:
// A count whose bytes no word holds is no length a list can have: a billion
// four-byte elements trap at the list's own precondition. On boot 5addc081
// the byte count wrapped, the allocation came back small, and the list
// answered a length of a billion over memory it did not own (exit 1, the
// host refusing a billion as an exit status).
fn main() = len(make_list(1000000000))
